WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.969 --> 00:00:06.359
It was close to a perfect night for the crowd
at the Lexington bar in Islington.

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:12.020
Here, in the north London constituency of
Labour leader, Jeremy Corbyn, many had just

00:00:12.020 --> 00:00:19.160
a glimmer of hope when the exit polls started
to trickle in.

00:00:19.160 --> 00:00:21.039
The mood soon changed.

00:00:21.039 --> 00:00:22.119
 

00:00:22.119 --> 00:00:23.199
"Positive!"

00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:24.279
"Magnificent."

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:26.000
"Wonderful!"

00:00:26.500 --> 00:00:30.089
"I'm feeling very pleased. Anything is better than a Tory majority."

00:00:30.089 --> 00:00:36.720
A hung parliament isn't ideal but then I'm
just happy that Labour are making some gains."

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.420
"It's disappointing to me, you could imagine
what would have happened if Labour had actually

00:00:42.420 --> 00:00:44.600
supported Jeremy Corbyn a lot earlier.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:48.570
Then we might have seen quite a substantial
Labour lead."

00:00:48.570 --> 00:00:53.320
Meanwhile, the business of counting ballots
got underway.

00:00:53.320 --> 00:01:00.070
Each vote checked by hand – like here in
Lambeth, a south London district.

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:05.990
And campaigners on the sidelines were already
taking stock.

00:01:05.990 --> 00:01:14.840
"It looks as though Theresa May has made a
bit of a blunder really in calling this election.

00:01:14.840 --> 00:01:19.040
I'm not entirely sure how she is getting on
with the rest of her party"

00:01:19.040 --> 00:01:20.480
"It has not been a brilliant night for us.

00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:26.630
I think our campaign could have been better,
I think everyone acknowledges that within

00:01:26.630 --> 00:01:28.960
the party.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:34.230
I think we could have talked more about the
things that we have done well over the past

00:01:34.230 --> 00:01:36.320
seven years."

00:01:36.320 --> 00:01:41.549
Back at The Lexington bar in Islington – cheering
and celebrations continued into the early

00:01:41.549 --> 00:01:42.630
hours.

00:01:42.630 --> 00:01:54.580
For these Labour supporters at least, it's
a vote to remember.

